!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/an-atom-construction-may-not-write-its-supertypes-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1"
  description: """
    The chain is `type`'s, which every type constructor composes, so every type body has the slot, an atom family's
    instance included -- and no declaration writes it. Construction transfers kind, not IS-A, so `age` built with
    `!integer_type` has an empty chain; one that IS-A `int32` is written `!int32 ^ { ... }`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
